<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kiliya</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Chilia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kiliya, Chilia in Romanian, is a town on the Chilia branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> delta in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>. A medieval trade port contested by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, Wallachia and Moldavia, it was taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-the-great">Stephen the Great</a> in 1465 and by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in 1484, cutting Moldavia off from the sea.</p></div>
